  "context_pill": "TDS Non-Compliance & Disallowance",
  "example_summary": "Delta Ltd. failed to deduct TDS on Salary and Directors' Remuneration in March 2026, leading to a 30% disallowance under Section 40(a)(ia).",
  "source_provision": "| Statutory Provision | Subject Matter | Threshold / Condition | Disallowance Rate |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Section 192 | Salary | Payment basis | 30% u/s 40(a)(ia) |\n| Section 194 | Directors' Remuneration | Credit/Payment whichever is earlier | 30% u/s 40(a)(ia) |\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Scope of Section 40(a)(ia): \nThis section applies to any sum payable to a resident on which tax is deductible under Chapter XVII-B. If TDS is not deducted, or after deduction is not remitted within the due date specified in Section 139(1), 30% of the amount is disallowed.\n\n> [!NOTE] Timing of Deduction:\nFor salary, the tax must be deducted at the time of payment. For directors' remuneration, the tax must be deducted at the time of credit to the payee's account or payment, whichever is earlier.",
